Tune LZMA literal contexts for the MIPS-heavy T33gs NOR rootfs.
The lc=0/lp=2 properties are supported by the existing kernel XZ decoder;
keep the encoder preset, dictionary size, block size and filters unchanged.
Measured RISC-V voice rootfs fixture: 12,591,104 -> 12,394,496 bytes.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board flash capacity]

--- a/squashfs-tools/xz_wrapper.c
+++ b/squashfs-tools/xz_wrapper.c
@@ -450,6 +450,10 @@
                 	goto failed;
 
 		stream->opt.dict_size = stream->dictionary_size;
+		/* MIPS instructions are four-byte aligned; retain the same
+		 * LZMA2 stream, decoder and dictionary with position contexts. */
+		stream->opt.lc = 0;
+		stream->opt.lp = 2;
 
 		filter->length = 0;
 		res = lzma_stream_buffer_encode(filter->filter,
